  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 236.18pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.224pt, 271.97pt, "Piezoelectric resonators have emerged as promising energy-storage elements for compact")
  #line-at(482.62pt, 271.97pt, "high-frequency ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 297.89pt, "DC-DC power converters. Still, practical implementation requires simultaneously high ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(451.78pt, 297.89pt, "𝑘")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(457.9pt, 300.29pt, "𝑡")
  #line-at(458.5pt, 293.81pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(463.42pt, 297.89pt, " (electromechanical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 323.45pt, "coupling), ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.1pt, 323.45pt, "Q")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(126.02pt, 323.45pt, " (high quality factor) and low resistance/impedance fluctuations. Spurious Lamb-wave and lateral ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 348.65pt, "modes are particularly problematic because they reduce the usable inductive frequency span and complicate ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 373.97pt, "converter operation over variable loads. Here we report a lithography-free, apodized 163° Y-cut lithium ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.29pt, "niobate thickness-shear resonator with reduced electrically visible spurious responses while preserving the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 424.63pt, "intrinsically large coupling of the thickness-shear mode. Finite-element simulations show that a square plate ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 449.95pt, "excites numerous lateral spurious modes near the principal shear resonance. In contrast, a curved asymmetric ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 475.15pt, "plate outline redistributes the lateral acoustic boundary conditions and reduces electrically visible spurious ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 500.47pt, "responses. Experiments on multiple resonator outlines, interconnection schemes, and device areas are ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 526.27pt, "performed to characterize the device responses. The representative 560 ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(411.31pt, 526.27pt, "mm")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(429.67pt, 522.19pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(436.39pt, 526.27pt, " device exhibits a series ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 551.83pt, "resonance near 3.67 MHz, an effective electromechanical coupling coefficient of 53.57%, a series quality ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 577.15pt, "factor of 1146, and a series resonance figure of merit of 614. A representative device fitted with a modified ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 602.5pt, "Butterworth-van Dyke equivalent circuit model shows excellent agreement between measurement and model, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 627.82pt, "with a maximum Bode quality factor of 2896. These results support lateral-boundary apodization as a practical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 653.02pt, "approach to high-coupling lithium niobate resonators with reduced electrically visible spurious responses for ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 678.34pt, "piezoelectric power converters. ")
]

