  #line-at(70.824pt, 72.72pt, "does not guarantee a suitable response for power conversion; narrow spurious modes can produce fluctuations ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 97.94pt, "in the real part of the impedance, R, and thereby increase resonator loss near the intended operating region. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 123.26pt, "Consequently, recent LN (lithium niobate) resonator research has increasingly focused on suppressing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 148.58pt, "spurious modes while retaining high coupling and low motional resistance. ")
  #line-at(85.224pt, 173.9pt, "Several design strategies have been developed to address this challenge. Braun et al. reported optimized ")
