  #line-at(85.224pt, 125.06pt, "To quantitatively compare the spurious response, the residual energy per MHz was extracted from the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 150.26pt, "resistance spectrum, as described in detail in Figs. S17-S19 in the Supplementary Information. This metric ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 175.58pt, "measures the integrated squared residual between the measured curve and the smooth main mode fitting curve, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 200.9pt, "normalized by the analyzed frequency span. Lower values indicate smaller resistance fluctuations relative to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 226.22pt, "the smooth main-mode response. Because the analysis contains user-defined valley/peak search windows and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 251.57pt, "an empirically constructed baseline, residual per MHz is treated as a comparative continuous metric rather ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 276.77pt, "than an absolute definition of a spurious-free resonator. ")
  #line-at(85.224pt, 302.09pt, "The present device shows a residual energy per MHz of 0.014, among the lowest values in the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 327.41pt, "benchmarked resistance spectra. The relative result remains robust under variations of the PCHIP baseline ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 352.73pt, "parameters, as detailed in the Supplementary Information. As an independent electrical cross-check, the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 378.05pt, "representative 560 mm² Shape-5 device also maintains an uninterrupted inductive interval of approximately ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 403.25pt, "723 kHz. Together with the high effective coupling and quality factor, these results support reduced ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 428.59pt, "electrically visible lateral-mode features in the shaped TS-mode LiNbO₃ resonator.  ")
