  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.224pt, 147.74pt, "The results support lateral-boundary apodization as an approach for reducing the electrically visible ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 173.06pt, "response of spurious modes in high-coupling TS-mode LiNbO₃ resonators. Unlike multi-finger excitation, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 198.38pt, "this approach leaves the active vertical electric field largely intact, thereby preserving the strong coupling of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 223.58pt, "the shear mode. The strategy is also compatible with a lithography-free fabrication flow because the resonator ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 248.93pt, "outline can be defined by laser cutting after blanket electrode deposition. This feature is useful for rapid design ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 274.25pt, "iteration and for large-area resonators intended for DC-DC power conversion, where fine lithographic ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 299.57pt, "patterning is costly and not always necessary. ")
  #line-at(85.224pt, 324.89pt, "One possible physical interpretation is the modification of lateral standing-wave boundary conditions. In ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 350.09pt, "square plates, long parallel edges allow many lateral modes to satisfy resonance conditions near the principal ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 375.41pt, "TS resonance. These modes are coupled to the electrical port and appear as spurious peaks and notches in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 400.73pt, "admittance. Curved and asymmetric boundaries alter lateral acoustic reflections, thereby reducing the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 426.07pt, "electrical visibility of unwanted modes. The finite-element mode shapes in Fig. 2 and the measured spectra in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 451.39pt, "Fig. 3 are consistent with this interpretation. The same-area simulation isolates boundary geometry within the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 476.59pt, "model; the fabricated contour, scaling, interconnection, and repeatability studies address complementary ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 501.91pt, "questions rather than constituting a controlled experimental geometric sensitivity study. An independently ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 527.23pt, "fabricated Shape-5 resonator reproduces the same overall electrical response, as shown in Figs. S13–S14 and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 552.55pt, "Table S8. ")
  #line-at(85.224pt, 577.87pt, "Packaging is a second critical factor. The strong improvement in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(372.19pt, 577.87pt, "Q")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.11pt, 577.87pt, " with increased wire bonding indicates ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 603.22pt, "that electrical access and boundary loading can limit the measured resonator performance. The interconnect ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 628.42pt, "must provide low series resistance while avoiding stiff or nonuniform mechanical constraints that can seed ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 653.74pt, "spurious modes or lead to anchor loss. The shaped devices with improved wire bonds achieve substantially ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 679.06pt, "higher ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(101.66pt, 679.06pt, "Q")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(109.58pt, 679.06pt, " than sparsely bonded devices, showing that intrinsic acoustic designs and package should be treated ")
]

