  #line-at(85.224pt, 269.33pt, "As shown in Fig. S2 in the Supplementary Information, 0.5 mm thick 163° Y-cut LiNbO₃ wafers were ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 294.65pt, "cleaned before metal deposition. Aluminum electrodes were deposited (1.0 μm) on the top and bottom surfaces ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 319.97pt, "to form a vertical electric-field excitation path. The resonator outlines were subsequently defined by UV ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 345.29pt, "excimer laser micromachining using an IPG IX-255 Excimer Laser Micromachining system (LMM-01, Singh ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 370.61pt, "Center for Nanotechnology) equipped with a 193 nm UV excimer laser. For through-cutting, the metallized ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 395.81pt, "LiNbO₃ samples were mounted on a sacrificial carrier wafer or aluminum sheet and secured during processing. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 421.15pt, "CAD-defined resonator outlines were cut using a nominal target energy of 7.0 mJ, a beam size of 10 × 10 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 446.47pt, "μm², a repetition rate of 800 Hz, a pulse spacing of 1.0 μm, and 30 passes per shape. This laser-cutting process ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 471.79pt, "enabled square and shaped plates to be realized without photolithographic patterning of the active resonator ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 497.11pt, "body. ")
