  #line-at(115.22pt, 374.57pt, " Summary of the lateral CAD geometries. *Straight-edge orientation is reported relative to the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 387.17pt, "local +x direction and reduced to 0–180°. These angles provide the explicit taper/edge-direction ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 400.01pt, "information needed to reproduce the polygonal portions of each outline. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 418.63pt, "Geometric design variables: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(206.09pt, 418.63pt, "The CAD comparison spans overall width/height, active plate area, perimeter, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 433.15pt, "straight-edge orientation, taper, concavity, and boundary curvature. These quantities are reported as ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 447.79pt, "geometric descriptors rather than as independently optimized variables. The present data provide a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 462.31pt, "qualitative boundary-selection rationale—reducing parallel reflection paths and introducing asymmetry—")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 476.83pt, "rather than a unique optimum set of radii or taper angles. A systematic one-variable-at-a-time sensitivity ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 491.35pt, "study or numerical objective-function optimization was not performed in the present work and should not be ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 505.87pt, "implied.")
  #line-at(112.34pt, 505.87pt, "A practical workflow is to select plate thickness and area, compare candidate contours under ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 520.51pt, "matched numerical conditions, and assess the fabricated device and its interconnections. ")
