// arXiv source page 29
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(307.49pt, 753.72pt, "7 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 72.72pt, "the main manuscript gives C₀ = 486 pF, Lm = 8.9 µH, Cm = 211 pF, and Rm = 0.155 Ω. Thus, resonator ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 97.94pt, "area should be selected jointly with capacitance, motional impedance, effective-inductance range, load ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 123.26pt, "range, and operating frequency rather than optimized independently. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 148.58pt, "Although the 560 mm² resonator has a relatively large lateral footprint, the active LiNbO₃ plate is only 0.5 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 173.9pt, "mm thick, corresponding to an active material volume of approximately 280 mm³ (0.28 cm³). For ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 199.22pt, "volumetric context, a representative commercial 33-µH high-current shielded power inductor (Coilcraft ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 224.42pt, "SER2918H-333KL) has maximum package dimensions of approximately 27.94 × 27.9 × 17.78 mm³, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 249.77pt, "corresponding to a geometric package envelope of approximately 13.9 cm³. On this limited active-plate-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 275.09pt, "versus-package-envelope basis, the piezoelectric plate is approximately 50 times smaller in volume. This ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 300.41pt, "comparison is intended only to illustrate the volumetric potential of the thin piezoelectric element and is not ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 325.73pt, "a claim of direct component or converter-level equivalence. The magnetic inductor and piezoelectric ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 351.05pt, "resonator differ in operating principle, current handling, energy storage, large-signal power capability, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 376.25pt, "thermal limits, and frequency dependence. In addition, the present PCB and wire-bond assembly was ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 401.57pt, "designed for laboratory characterization rather than minimum footprint. We therefore do not claim a 50× ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 426.91pt, "reduction in total packaged component volume; minimizing the complete footprint requires further ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 452.23pt, "resonator–package–converter co-design. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 477.55pt, "Expected converter power density is likewise not inferred from the present small-signal S-parameter ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 502.75pt, "measurements. The source-level sweep provides an excitation-sensitivity check over the measured range, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 528.07pt, "but a defensible converter-level power-density estimate requires sustained large-signal characterization of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 553.39pt, "resonator voltage and current, transferred and dissipated power, self-heating, nonlinear loss, contact ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 578.71pt, "reliability, thermal limits, and the area/volume of the complete converter implementation. The present ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 604.06pt, "results therefore establish the resonator-level area–impedance–loss trade-off, while converter-level power ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 629.38pt, "density remains a subject for future system-level validation. ")
]

